    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d630-a2">

                <pb facs="0752" n="692" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg692"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Extract from letter of Mr. James R. Bain, purser of
                        British steamship Engineer, to Mr. Consul St. John.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-19"><hi rendition="#small-caps">March</hi> 19,
                        1895</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Shortly after 7 a.m. on the 12th instant, while stepping onto the wharves, in the
                    discharge of my duty as purser, I was shot and wounded in several parts of my
                    head and in my right arm by a body of men armed with rifles, shotguns, and
                    revolvers, who, without provocation or warning, came up the wharves and attacked
                    me and the laborers at said steamship.</p>
                <p>I was unconscious and sent to the hospital, where I have been under treatment of
                    the doctors and have suffered and still suffer much from my wounds. One of the
                    shot entered above my right eye and lodged behind it and can not be extracted,
                    and it may yet cause me the loss of the sight of that eye.</p>
                <p>Considering my hospital expenses, the wantonness of the attack, and the suffering
                    I have had to endure and still endure from my wounds, I consider that I am
                    entitled to compensation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James H. Bain</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Purser of the British steamship
                        Engineer.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
